.TH RF-PASTE 1 "August 2026" "rf-clipboard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rf-paste \- paste from an encrypted shared clipboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rf-paste
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rf-paste
downloads the shared clipboard, decrypts it locally, and writes the
plaintext to standard output. It is the counterpart of
.BR rf-clip (1),
which copies standard input to the clipboard.
.PP
Exits non-zero with a message on stderr if the clipboard is empty or the
content cannot be decrypted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
$ rf-paste
$ rf-paste > file.txt
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rf-clip (1),
.BR rf-copy (1)
